.TH COMPUTERMOVIE 1
.SH NAME
computermovie \- keyframed camera flythrough demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreammachines/computermovie
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Computermovie
is a work-alike of the "computer movies" chapter of Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
early computer animation built from a camera path keyframed through a
static synthetic scene, interpolated and played back frame by frame,
rather than the scene itself moving.
.PP
Six coloured panels are arranged in a row; a five-keyframe, 16-second
looping camera path (linearly interpolating position and yaw/pitch
between keyframes) flies the viewpoint through them, with the current
time and camera position/orientation shown as an overlay. The path
repeats indefinitely; press
.B q
or Escape to quit.
.PP
Contrast
.IR draw3ddemo (1),
where the object spins in place and the camera never moves.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/dreammachines/computermovie.b
.br
.B /module/math/camerapath.m
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw3ddemo (1)
